WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.716
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 3: Fun and Games.

2
00:00:03.796 --> 00:00:10.778
In this unit you will learn the words for games
and play, like bounce, roll, throw and catch.

3
00:00:10.858 --> 00:00:18.902
You will name the parts of your body, and learn the
words that say where something is — on, under, next to,

4
00:00:18.982 --> 00:00:20.041
left and right.

5
00:00:20.121 --> 00:00:26.799
You will play simple games, try a game from
another country, and listen to a funny story.

6
00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:31.355
You will also hear the short 'u' sound in sun, fun and duck.

7
00:00:31.435 --> 00:00:34.392
Learn by playing — that is the best way.

8
00:00:34.472 --> 00:00:40.770
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:49.033
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
act out ball actions (bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit).

10
00:00:49.113 --> 00:00:54.871
You will also name parts of the body
(hand, foot, ear, nose, shoulder, head…)

11
00:00:54.951 --> 00:01:01.087
You will also say where something is (on,
under, next to) and show left and right.

12
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.892
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:03.972 --> 00:01:09.949
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit, run.

14
00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:16.224
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

15
00:01:16.304 --> 00:01:22.290
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Big Ball and Talk about Fun and Games.

16
00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:27.531
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

17
00:01:27.611 --> 00:01:32.024
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

18
00:01:32.104 --> 00:01:36.418
The first language focus is Tell what you can do at play.

19
00:01:36.498 --> 00:01:39.269
Choose a game action you are good at.

20
00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:42.815
Say the sentence, then show it with your body.

21
00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:47.825
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:47.905 --> 00:01:52.239
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:52.319 --> 00:01:55.858
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:01:55.938 --> 00:02:03.240
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.940
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:12.109
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:02:12.189 --> 00:02:19.425
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
